Feature: Standing orders
  A commander can give a drone a [[standing order]] with its order. The standing order says what
  the drone does if it is out of contact for some time. It is the answer to a question that the
  commander cannot ask later: the radio shadow of an enemy tower cuts the link, and the drone
  flies alone.

  Without a standing order, a drone that loses its link flies home. It also flies home when it
  is out of contact and its [[battery]] gets down to 60 s: that is enough to fly home. With a standing order, it
  does what the commander planned. It stays on that order, also when it is in contact again,
  until the commander gives it a new order.

  Expectation: A drone out of contact keeps its order until the standing order is due
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
    And the standing order of the first Blue drone is hold after 5 s
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 3 seconds
    Then the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower

  Expectation: A drone out of contact does what its standing order says
    Overrides: A drone out of contact keeps its order until the standing order is due
    The standing order is due 5 s after the link is cut.

    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
    And the standing order of the first Blue drone is hold after 5 s
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the order that the first Blue drone flies is hold

  Expectation: A drone with no standing order flies home when its link is lost
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
    And the standing order of the first Blue drone is none
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 30 seconds
    Then the order that the first Blue drone flies is go home

  Expectation: A drone with a standing order does not fly home when its link is lost
    Overrides: A drone with no standing order flies home when its link is lost
    The standing order is the plan of the commander. It replaces the failsafe.

    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
    And the standing order of the first Blue drone is hold after 5 s
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 30 seconds
    Then the order that the first Blue drone flies is hold

  Expectation: A drone stays on its standing order when it is in contact again
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
    And the standing order of the first Blue drone is go home after 5 s
    When the first Blue drone flies through the radio shadow for 10 seconds
    Then the order that the first Blue drone flies is go home

  Expectation: A new order replaces the standing order
    Given the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
    And the standing order of the first Blue drone is hold after 5 s
    When the first Blue drone is given the order to hold
    Then the standing order of the first Blue drone is none

  Expectation: A drone with no standing order flies home when its battery is low
    Given the batteries are on
    And the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
    And the standing order of the first Blue drone is none
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 70 s
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 15 seconds
    Then the order that the first Blue drone flies is go home

  Expectation: A standing order replaces the flight home at a low battery
    Overrides: A drone with no standing order flies home when its battery is low
    The commander takes the risk. The standing order is not due for 30 s.

    Given the batteries are on
    And the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
    And the standing order of the first Blue drone is hold after 30 s
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 70 s
    And the first Blue drone is near the Red home tower
    When the game runs for 15 seconds
    Then the order that the first Blue drone flies is take the west tower
